1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,628
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,712 --> 00:00:08,216
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,967 --> 00:00:10,802
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:12,971
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:19,060
Where is my father?

7
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:20,729
Why aren't you with him?

8
00:00:20,812 --> 00:00:22,897
You don't have a father! Okay?

9
00:00:22,981 --> 00:00:25,817
Do you want Tatoy instead?

10
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,193
[Mercado] <i>You have a follow-up mission.</i>

11
00:00:27,277 --> 00:00:28,737
[Atoy] <i>This is the device I extracted</i>

12
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:30,655
<i>from the Zahran embassy, sir.</i>
<i>Why is it here again?</i>

13
00:00:30,739 --> 00:00:34,034
<i>This laptop is for your safekeeping</i>

14
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:37,704
<i>until you find Ms. Lily Santiago,</i>

15
00:00:37,787 --> 00:00:40,331
<i>who is in charge of this device.</i>

16
00:00:40,415 --> 00:00:41,416
[in English] You're the Master Cutter?!

17
00:00:41,499 --> 00:00:43,168
Master Cutter, help us!

18
00:00:43,251 --> 00:00:44,669
Oh, oh. No, I'm not.

19
00:00:44,753 --> 00:00:50,341
We're administrators
of the Build for Kids organization.

20
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:52,552
The money we saved was stolen.

21
00:00:52,635 --> 00:00:57,182
We'll try to contact another tracker.

22
00:00:57,265 --> 00:01:00,477
Uh, maybe he can help you.

23
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:02,896
Please stop crying. Stop crying.

24
00:01:02,979 --> 00:01:05,106
[Cita] Huh? Who?

25
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:07,358
- The… The son…
- [quirky sting]

26
00:01:07,442 --> 00:01:09,152
Son of a thread.

27
00:01:09,235 --> 00:01:12,280
[Atoy] <i>Observe how the theft happened,</i>

28
00:01:12,363 --> 00:01:14,074
<i>how they entered the place.</i>

29
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:15,784
Just trust, and…

30
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:17,285
I'll bring them their karma.

31
00:01:17,368 --> 00:01:20,246
[vendor] <i>But Olga never told us</i>
<i>she had a missing child.</i>

32
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:23,166
Don't talk to gossips.

33
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:26,336
Who else knows about the money here?

34
00:01:26,419 --> 00:01:28,922
The ex-president of Build for Kids.

35
00:01:29,005 --> 00:01:30,632
[Emerson] <i>Kevin Martinez.</i>

36
00:01:30,715 --> 00:01:32,550
[Ame] You're acting
like the Master Cutter.

37
00:01:32,634 --> 00:01:34,803
Atoy's level is way up here.

38
00:01:34,886 --> 00:01:36,471
Yours is way down here!

39
00:01:36,554 --> 00:01:37,555
[Kurt] <i>Do you have a mission?</i>

40
00:01:38,181 --> 00:01:39,516
<i>But Atoy isn't here, right?</i>

41
00:01:39,599 --> 00:01:41,851
PREVIOUSLY

42
00:01:41,935 --> 00:01:43,478
[music swells]

43
00:01:43,561 --> 00:01:45,313
♪ <i>Fix this</i> ♪

44
00:01:47,607 --> 00:01:49,567
So, what? Let's go, girls?

45
00:01:49,651 --> 00:01:50,693
[in English] Let's go.

46
00:01:50,777 --> 00:01:53,154
["In Nothing" by Wickermoss
with Neth Macam playing]

47
00:01:53,238 --> 00:01:54,155
It's safe now.

48
00:01:56,741 --> 00:01:58,409
Why are we hiding from Cathy?

49
00:02:00,829 --> 00:02:02,372
I'm just avoiding the issue.

50
00:02:03,373 --> 00:02:05,583
I don't want Cathy and I
to fight because of you.

51
00:02:06,709 --> 00:02:10,004
Because you're both important to me.

52
00:02:11,297 --> 00:02:12,382
Really?

53
00:02:18,555 --> 00:02:20,640
[music fades]

54
00:02:20,723 --> 00:02:23,059
[suave theme music playing]

55
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:27,230
[motorcycle revving]

56
00:02:27,313 --> 00:02:29,149
[sewing machine whirring]

57
00:02:29,232 --> 00:02:30,108
[scratches]

58
00:02:30,191 --> 00:02:31,693
[snipping]

59
00:02:31,776 --> 00:02:33,611
[clacking]

60
00:02:33,695 --> 00:02:35,029
[sewing machine clacking]

61
00:02:35,113 --> 00:02:36,656
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

62
00:02:36,739 --> 00:02:39,534
[gunshots]

63
00:02:39,617 --> 00:02:41,536
[clicking]

64
00:02:41,619 --> 00:02:44,247
[snipping]

65
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:46,332
[music swells]

66
00:02:49,043 --> 00:02:50,628
[music fades]

67
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:53,882
[coughing]

68
00:02:55,049 --> 00:02:56,259
What are you all doing here?

69
00:02:57,010 --> 00:02:58,303
Why are you all crowding?

70
00:02:58,386 --> 00:03:00,138
[T-bak] You're cold, huh?

71
00:03:00,221 --> 00:03:01,764
The sun's blazing!

72
00:03:01,848 --> 00:03:03,433
[chuckles]

73
00:03:03,516 --> 00:03:06,019
I know. You're kissing!

74
00:03:06,102 --> 00:03:08,479
No, we're not! Your mouth is sleazy.

75
00:03:08,563 --> 00:03:10,815
I just said you're kissing,
I'm sleazy already?

76
00:03:11,357 --> 00:03:12,609
Sleazy is being naked!

77
00:03:12,692 --> 00:03:15,278
And besides, it's sweet!

78
00:03:15,361 --> 00:03:17,947
No. I didn't kiss Karla.

79
00:03:18,031 --> 00:03:19,949
- I have a girlfriend.
- [T-bak] Ouch.

80
00:03:22,076 --> 00:03:22,952
Yes.

81
00:03:24,078 --> 00:03:26,039
I'll just go see Cathy.

82
00:03:26,122 --> 00:03:28,249
[gentle music playing]

83
00:03:32,086 --> 00:03:33,212
That hurts.

84
00:03:34,088 --> 00:03:35,548
- Shut up.
- [groans]

85
00:03:36,132 --> 00:03:38,509
- You're irritating.
- [T-Bak] It hurts. [sighs]

86
00:03:39,552 --> 00:03:42,597
Gavin, ouch.

87
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:46,351
[Denden] Uncle, where could Emerson be?

88
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:48,811
He's not at his shop.

89
00:03:48,895 --> 00:03:50,313
And it's still not fixed.

90
00:03:50,396 --> 00:03:51,481
- Oh.
- Maybe he moved?

91
00:03:51,564 --> 00:03:53,149
He's with Atoy.

92
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:55,485
But don't bother him because

93
00:03:55,568 --> 00:03:58,154
- he's frustrated.
- [in English] Because?

94
00:03:58,238 --> 00:04:00,657
Because he's looking for someone.

95
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:02,659
But he doesn't know how to do it.

96
00:04:03,368 --> 00:04:04,869
Is it a woman?

97
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:07,497
Oh, no, he's still looking
for someone else. I'm here, though.

98
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:10,291
Oh, Denden. Behave yourself!

99
00:04:10,375 --> 00:04:12,627
You should play a little hard to get.

100
00:04:12,710 --> 00:04:15,296
Like a Filipina maiden.

101
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:17,548
A Filipina maiden? How's that?

102
00:04:18,216 --> 00:04:19,300
[Denden] Hard to get?

103
00:04:19,384 --> 00:04:21,052
Will he like me if…

104
00:04:21,135 --> 00:04:22,887
[suspicious music playing]

105
00:04:24,973 --> 00:04:26,307
[Denden] I act like
a Filipina maiden, fine.

106
00:04:26,391 --> 00:04:28,434
[dramatic sting]

107
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:32,939
[Denden] I'll learn how to be one.

108
00:04:33,022 --> 00:04:33,898
[Denden giggles]

109
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:35,733
[dramatic stinging]

110
00:04:37,568 --> 00:04:40,238
Uncle, you're not listening to me.

111
00:04:40,321 --> 00:04:41,864
I've been talking nonstop.

112
00:04:42,699 --> 00:04:43,866
Thank you.

113
00:04:47,161 --> 00:04:50,290
Ah, brother, that man who just left.

114
00:04:50,373 --> 00:04:51,749
Do you know him?

115
00:04:51,833 --> 00:04:53,209
Ah, that's Boyet.

116
00:04:53,751 --> 00:04:56,379
- Boyet.
- Yes, that's his place.

117
00:04:56,462 --> 00:04:58,172
Ah, just there?

118
00:04:58,256 --> 00:04:59,299
Just there.

119
00:05:00,049 --> 00:05:01,009
[in English] Okay.

120
00:05:02,176 --> 00:05:03,511
- [in English] Thank you.
- [Malou on the phone] <i>Sir Emerson,</i>

121
00:05:03,594 --> 00:05:04,429
<i>you called?</i>

122
00:05:04,512 --> 00:05:06,097
<i>Any update on our case?</i>

123
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:09,142
Uh, Ma'am Malou, yes, uh…

124
00:05:09,225 --> 00:05:12,437
Well, um… Uh…

125
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:14,022
[Odette on phone] <i>Did you catch the thief?</i>

126
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:15,440
<i>Was the money recovered?!</i>

127
00:05:15,523 --> 00:05:17,650
<i>The son of the thread is amazing!</i>

128
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:20,945
[in English] Wa, wa…
Wait, wait, wait. Wait, ma'am.

129
00:05:21,029 --> 00:05:22,613
[titters] Uh, just relax.

130
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:25,450
Um, well, that's what
I wanted to tell you,

131
00:05:25,533 --> 00:05:28,411
about the mission
and the son of the thread.

132
00:05:28,494 --> 00:05:30,288
- Emerson! Emerson!
- [indistinct]

133
00:05:30,371 --> 00:05:32,457
- It seems like… Wait… wait, wait, wait.
- [huffs]

134
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:33,458
This is important.

135
00:05:33,541 --> 00:05:35,084
- Brother Kurt, I'm on the phone.
- [huffs]

136
00:05:35,168 --> 00:05:37,128
It's about your mission!

137
00:05:37,211 --> 00:05:41,799
- [Emerson] Wha-- What?
- I saw the thief on the CCTV!

138
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:43,468
- [Kurt] Yes!
- How--

139
00:05:43,551 --> 00:05:44,802
How can you be sure?

140
00:05:44,886 --> 00:05:46,804
I saw it in the footage.

141
00:05:46,888 --> 00:05:49,640
He stretched his hands in a strange way.

142
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:51,642
And… [chuckles]

143
00:05:51,726 --> 00:05:54,812
the diamond tattoos on his fingers!

144
00:05:54,896 --> 00:05:57,190
Oh, didn't you notice that?

145
00:05:57,273 --> 00:05:59,817
Uh, what? I noticed them too.

146
00:05:59,901 --> 00:06:02,278
Hmm, you. I was
just testing you, of course.

147
00:06:02,361 --> 00:06:06,074
Anyway, I saw that man
at the fishball stand earlier,

148
00:06:06,157 --> 00:06:08,910
and I know where he's going.

149
00:06:08,993 --> 00:06:10,536
- Ah. Mm-hmm.
- Really? Really?

150
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:11,454
- Wait, wait, wait.
- Yes.

151
00:06:11,537 --> 00:06:14,749
Yes. Hello, he… Ma'am? Ma'am? Hello.

152
00:06:14,832 --> 00:06:16,501
Ah, Ma'am Malou, yes.

153
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:18,419
Here's the update.

154
00:06:18,503 --> 00:06:20,421
We have a lead. [chuckles]

155
00:06:20,505 --> 00:06:22,465
So, just relax, ma'am.

156
00:06:22,548 --> 00:06:27,011
Sit tight, and the son of the thread
will handle this.

157
00:06:27,095 --> 00:06:28,930
[in English] Okay, ma'am? All right!

158
00:06:29,013 --> 00:06:32,016
Thank you! Bye-bye.

159
00:06:32,725 --> 00:06:35,394
[giggles]

160
00:06:35,478 --> 00:06:37,396
Awesome, awesome. Okay.

161
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:39,732
Let's go. Let's check it out.
This is exciting.

162
00:06:39,816 --> 00:06:44,195
It's like we're…
I'm Atoy, and you're the sidekick.

163
00:06:44,278 --> 00:06:45,613
Why am I the sidekick?

164
00:06:45,696 --> 00:06:47,156
I found the suspect!

165
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:48,783
That was just luck!

166
00:06:48,866 --> 00:06:50,952
I'll show you later,
I'll handle the strategy.

167
00:06:51,035 --> 00:06:53,037
[in English] I'll show you.

168
00:06:53,121 --> 00:06:54,163
Let's go. Let's check it out.

169
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:55,331
- Okay.
- Let's go.

170
00:06:55,414 --> 00:06:58,793
[sneaky music playing]

171
00:07:03,131 --> 00:07:05,216
That's where Boyet works.

172
00:07:05,299 --> 00:07:07,093
That's what the fishball vendor said.

173
00:07:18,646 --> 00:07:19,647
[in English] Oh, affirmative.

174
00:07:20,857 --> 00:07:23,151
Looks like this is our suspect.

175
00:07:23,985 --> 00:07:26,863
So, what's our next step?

176
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:29,615
[in English] Hmm, call a friend.

177
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:31,117
[music fades]

178
00:07:33,202 --> 00:07:35,121
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

179
00:07:39,792 --> 00:07:42,628
[phone ringing]

180
00:07:44,630 --> 00:07:45,465
Hello?

181
00:07:46,048 --> 00:07:47,383
What now?

182
00:07:47,967 --> 00:07:49,010
[in English] Good news.

183
00:07:49,844 --> 00:07:53,431
We found the suspect
in the theft of five million.

184
00:07:53,514 --> 00:07:55,683
[smirks] Nice, huh.

185
00:07:56,559 --> 00:07:57,477
[in English] Okay.

186
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:59,520
In fairness, you're good.

187
00:07:59,604 --> 00:08:00,980
Of course. You know me.

188
00:08:01,063 --> 00:08:03,149
Ah, Atoy, Atoy! This is Brother Kurt.

189
00:08:03,232 --> 00:08:04,233
I'm the one who found him.

190
00:08:04,317 --> 00:08:05,651
This is Brother Kurt.

191
00:08:05,735 --> 00:08:08,029
Fine. Ah, fine, fine.

192
00:08:08,112 --> 00:08:09,238
Brother Kurt?

193
00:08:10,615 --> 00:08:12,742
[smirks] That explains it.

194
00:08:13,951 --> 00:08:15,745
But I'm wondering, Atoy,

195
00:08:16,662 --> 00:08:17,788
if he has five million,

196
00:08:17,872 --> 00:08:19,624
why is he still vulcanizing at that shop?

197
00:08:19,707 --> 00:08:21,209
[suspicious music playing]

198
00:08:21,292 --> 00:08:23,044
Because if it were me, I'd buy a fancy car

199
00:08:23,127 --> 00:08:24,879
and a nice house.

200
00:08:24,962 --> 00:08:26,631
I would just relax.

201
00:08:26,714 --> 00:08:28,132
YOLO, right?

202
00:08:28,841 --> 00:08:31,177
That means the five million isn't his.

203
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:34,013
He's giving the money to someone else.

204
00:08:34,096 --> 00:08:35,348
[in English] My thoughts exactly.

205
00:08:36,682 --> 00:08:38,184
Oh, so you're the best.

206
00:08:38,267 --> 00:08:39,268
[Atoy on phone] <i>Here's what you do.</i>

207
00:08:39,352 --> 00:08:42,188
The important thing to do
is go to that shop.

208
00:08:42,271 --> 00:08:44,232
[Atoy on phone] <i>Pretend to be customers</i>
<i>or whatever you want.</i>

209
00:08:44,315 --> 00:08:45,858
The important thing is, get inside,

210
00:08:45,942 --> 00:08:47,777
and gather information

211
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:49,320
about the money from that person.

212
00:08:49,403 --> 00:08:52,740
Just make sure you don't get detected.

213
00:08:52,823 --> 00:08:54,075
- [in English] G.
- [in English] Okay.

214
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:56,160
Let's go.

215
00:08:57,411 --> 00:08:58,538
Here's the plan.

216
00:08:59,247 --> 00:09:02,083
I'll be Mateo.

217
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:07,129
I'm the new up-and-coming race car driver.

218
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:10,132
I'll use an Italian accent.

219
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:12,176
Um…

220
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:15,346
[in Italian accent] Goodbye. Goodbye.

221
00:09:15,429 --> 00:09:17,139
- Hmm?
- Feels like I need a mustache.

222
00:09:17,223 --> 00:09:19,016
Oh. You even have a backstory?

223
00:09:19,892 --> 00:09:22,228
But you forgot the most important part.

224
00:09:22,770 --> 00:09:24,105
What?

225
00:09:24,855 --> 00:09:27,692
We need a tire to vulcanize.

226
00:09:27,775 --> 00:09:30,069
[sneaky music playing]

227
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:34,115
- Wow. Impressive.
- Right?

228
00:09:34,198 --> 00:09:35,324
[in English] Very good.

229
00:09:35,408 --> 00:09:38,911
I was just testing
if you really learned from Atoy.

230
00:09:38,995 --> 00:09:40,621
[in English] Hmm. But…

231
00:09:41,163 --> 00:09:43,708
Where are we going to get the bike tire?

232
00:09:44,792 --> 00:09:45,626
[clicks tongue]

233
00:09:46,377 --> 00:09:49,338
- So, we'll think of a way…
- [Karla] Brother! How are you?

234
00:09:49,422 --> 00:09:51,090
- What are you doing here?
- [Emerson mutters]

235
00:09:51,173 --> 00:09:53,092
[in Italian] Silence. Silence.

236
00:09:53,175 --> 00:09:54,760
Uh, hmm…

237
00:09:56,429 --> 00:09:57,471
Aha!

238
00:09:57,555 --> 00:09:59,348
Oh, give me the ball.

239
00:09:59,849 --> 00:10:00,725
Hmm?

240
00:10:01,726 --> 00:10:03,144
[Karla] What are you going to do?

241
00:10:03,227 --> 00:10:04,353
[Emerson] Just trust me.

242
00:10:05,104 --> 00:10:06,439
Hey, brother! I just bought that!

243
00:10:06,522 --> 00:10:07,690
That ball was expensive!

244
00:10:07,773 --> 00:10:09,984
- [hushing]
- [in Italian] Understood. Understood.

245
00:10:10,693 --> 00:10:12,778
I'll replace it later.

246
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:17,325
We need it for our operation

247
00:10:17,408 --> 00:10:21,287
surveillance, care of the children
of the thread.

248
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:23,539
Surveillance? Are you pretending
to be monsters?

249
00:10:24,206 --> 00:10:26,167
Who are the children of the thread?

250
00:10:26,250 --> 00:10:27,501
Just keep quiet.

251
00:10:27,585 --> 00:10:30,212
Just keep quiet. Don't…

252
00:10:34,383 --> 00:10:36,344
[barista, in English]
Cafe Americano for Atoy.

253
00:10:37,053 --> 00:10:39,096
- [barista, in English] Americano for Atoy.
- Atoy?

254
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:40,389
- [man, in English] Good morning.
- [barista, in English] Atoy, sir?

255
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:41,724
[in English] Yes.

256
00:10:41,807 --> 00:10:42,850
[Atoy, in English] Thank you.

257
00:10:44,101 --> 00:10:47,563
[pensive music playing]

258
00:11:02,244 --> 00:11:03,245
[Samir, in English] Ms. Audrey.

259
00:11:04,163 --> 00:11:06,123
[music fades]

260
00:11:06,207 --> 00:11:08,334
[in English] Samir, from the embassy.

261
00:11:08,417 --> 00:11:10,086
[in English] Yes, I remember.

262
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:12,296
[in English] Samir, hi.

263
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:13,714
[in English] May I?

264
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:16,801
Um…

265
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:22,515
[suspicious music playing]

266
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:27,561
[clears throat]

267
00:11:27,645 --> 00:11:29,605
[music fades]

268
00:11:30,689 --> 00:11:33,109
There, Italian. Got it.

269
00:11:33,192 --> 00:11:35,111
[clears throat]

270
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:38,906
[in Italian] Hello. Goodbye.

271
00:11:38,989 --> 00:11:40,533
[in Spanish] <i>Hasta la vista!</i> [titters]

272
00:11:40,616 --> 00:11:42,368
[speaking indistinctly in a vague accent]

273
00:11:42,451 --> 00:11:44,036
Um, Mateo.

274
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:47,998
[speaking indistinctly in a vague accent]

275
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:51,085
Pa-- Patch! No, um, uh--

276
00:11:51,168 --> 00:11:53,671
The… The hole. The… The strong kick!

277
00:11:53,754 --> 00:11:55,381
[stuttering]

278
00:11:55,464 --> 00:11:58,551
The ball, the hole, ah… patch!

279
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:01,762
[smirks, in Italian] Yes.

280
00:12:01,846 --> 00:12:02,888
[Emerson, in Italian] Yes.

281
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:04,765
- Hmm…
- [Emerson] Hmm?

282
00:12:04,849 --> 00:12:07,017
- [in Italian] Fifty.
- [in Italian] Fifty?

283
00:12:09,145 --> 00:12:10,312
Too expensive.

284
00:12:11,063 --> 00:12:12,398
No, I'm Filipino too.

285
00:12:12,481 --> 00:12:15,484
- And can't you lower it to 30?
- [quirky sting]

286
00:12:15,568 --> 00:12:17,695
- Fine.
- [Emerson] You can?

287
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:18,612
Okay, 30.

288
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:21,574
[in Italian] Goodbye.

289
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:22,867
[chuckles]

290
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:24,910
[in Italian] Yes.

291
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:28,706
[sneaky music playing]

292
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:33,419
[Emerson] Oh, ah! See, uh, hmm.

293
00:12:33,961 --> 00:12:36,422
- Diamond.
- [Boyet chuckles]

294
00:12:36,505 --> 00:12:38,132
- [chuckles]
- Truly diamond.

295
00:12:38,215 --> 00:12:40,551
Ah, tattoo.

296
00:12:41,635 --> 00:12:43,679
- [phone ringing]
- [suspicious music playing]

297
00:12:46,974 --> 00:12:47,892
[Boyet grunts]

298
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:50,311
- Wait a moment.
- [chuckles]

299
00:12:50,394 --> 00:12:52,521
- [in Italian] Yes, uh…
- [in English] Hello, boss!

300
00:12:53,272 --> 00:12:56,358
Yes. Your suitcase is here.

301
00:13:02,531 --> 00:13:04,283
‪[dramatic sting, music intensifies]

302
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:13,459
[in English] Hello, boss.

303
00:13:14,543 --> 00:13:16,545
Your suitcase is here.

304
00:13:17,338 --> 00:13:19,548
The money is safe, don't worry.

305
00:13:21,509 --> 00:13:23,010
[inhales, grunts]

306
00:13:33,062 --> 00:13:35,064
[Boyet] If you want, boss,
I can even take a picture of it.

307
00:13:35,773 --> 00:13:37,483
[clicks tongue] Don't worry.

308
00:13:37,566 --> 00:13:38,901
I won't steal from you.

309
00:13:41,737 --> 00:13:43,739
So, boss? Do you want me to count it?

310
00:13:47,326 --> 00:13:49,662
By the way, boss, where are we meeting?

311
00:13:55,501 --> 00:13:57,336
Yes! I'm not stupid.

312
00:13:57,419 --> 00:13:58,921
[music fades]

313
00:13:59,004 --> 00:14:00,798
Ten o'clock in the morning.

314
00:14:00,881 --> 00:14:04,593
7176!RbSbOlive Function Hall,
Athena Hotel.

315
00:14:04,677 --> 00:14:06,387
[suspicious music playing]

316
00:14:06,971 --> 00:14:10,432
As long as my share is complete, boss,
we won't have any problem.

317
00:14:12,768 --> 00:14:13,602
‪[sniffles]

318
00:14:16,438 --> 00:14:19,275
[music concludes]

319
00:14:29,827 --> 00:14:30,744
[Boyet] Who's there?

320
00:14:32,663 --> 00:14:35,958
Come out if you don't want to get hurt.

321
00:14:36,709 --> 00:14:40,629
[music swells]

322
00:14:44,049 --> 00:14:45,384
Who's there?!

323
00:14:54,268 --> 00:14:56,145
[tense music playing]

324
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:03,193
[Kurt] Oh!

325
00:15:03,277 --> 00:15:04,945
Hello!

326
00:15:05,029 --> 00:15:06,030
Uh, who are you?

327
00:15:06,113 --> 00:15:07,740
[in English] Ah, I come in peace.

328
00:15:08,699 --> 00:15:10,075
I'm not a bad person.

329
00:15:10,826 --> 00:15:13,287
[in English] Actually,
I'm a vlogger. [chuckles]

330
00:15:14,538 --> 00:15:16,290
- [Boyet, in English] Vlogger.
- [Kurt, in English] Yes.

331
00:15:16,373 --> 00:15:18,125
[ominous music playing]

332
00:15:20,878 --> 00:15:21,837
[Boyet] What do you need?

333
00:15:21,921 --> 00:15:26,425
Well, I just wanted to feature your shop.

334
00:15:26,508 --> 00:15:27,384
It looks great.

335
00:15:27,468 --> 00:15:30,846
Uh, what do you do here?

336
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:33,307
Who are your usual customers?

337
00:15:33,390 --> 00:15:34,725
- [Boyet chuckles]
- [indistinct]

338
00:15:34,808 --> 00:15:36,727
- [Boyet] Yes, yes.
- [Kurt] We'll feature everything!

339
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:38,145
[Boyet] Those rims are cheap.

340
00:15:38,228 --> 00:15:40,189
- They look great.
- Tomorrow, the branded ones will arrive.

341
00:15:40,272 --> 00:15:42,858
Wow, so many rims here, bro.

342
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:43,901
Game!

343
00:15:44,526 --> 00:15:46,528
But wait.

344
00:15:47,237 --> 00:15:49,073
Is there a fee for this?

345
00:15:49,156 --> 00:15:49,990
Fee?

346
00:15:51,075 --> 00:15:52,284
None.

347
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:54,286
Just a shout-out.

348
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:56,080
[in English] Shout-out?

349
00:15:56,789 --> 00:15:58,248
Fine, you may leave now.

350
00:15:58,332 --> 00:16:00,250
- Ah, okay.
- You're wasting my time.

351
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:02,294
[in English] Okay. Sorry, sorry.

352
00:16:02,378 --> 00:16:03,671
[in English] Thank you for your time.

353
00:16:03,754 --> 00:16:05,881
[tense music playing]

354
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:23,190
[suspicious music playing]

355
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:28,404
Brother Kurt, thank you so much earlier.

356
00:16:28,487 --> 00:16:29,863
You saved me there.

357
00:16:29,947 --> 00:16:33,200
Boyet really looked ready
to pull something shady.

358
00:16:33,283 --> 00:16:35,119
- Oh, it's nothing!
- Come on!

359
00:16:35,202 --> 00:16:37,246
Well, you disappeared for so long.

360
00:16:37,329 --> 00:16:40,290
I thought you got into trouble.

361
00:16:40,958 --> 00:16:41,875
[Emerson] Mmm.

362
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:44,962
Did you get anything
from risking your life there?

363
00:16:46,171 --> 00:16:48,257
Of course!

364
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:51,593
I saw the five million myself
inside the suitcase.

365
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:53,554
- [in English] Five million?!
- Yes!

366
00:16:53,637 --> 00:16:54,471
Incredible!

367
00:16:54,555 --> 00:16:58,851
He said he'll turn it over tomorrow,

368
00:16:59,643 --> 00:17:04,773
at the Athena Hotel, Olive Function Room.

369
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:06,316
[in English] At 10 a.m.

370
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:07,901
Let me check.

371
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:10,404
[in English] Mm, Athena Hotel.

372
00:17:10,487 --> 00:17:11,655
That's it, brother.

373
00:17:12,448 --> 00:17:14,575
There's an auction tomorrow morning.

374
00:17:14,658 --> 00:17:16,118
At the Olive Function Room.

375
00:17:16,201 --> 00:17:19,663
That's it, that's it.
That's where Boyet will go tomorrow.

376
00:17:19,747 --> 00:17:21,665
That's where he'll meet his Boss KM.

377
00:17:21,749 --> 00:17:23,125
Boss KM, Boss KM.

378
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:25,002
- Who could that be?
- Ouch.

379
00:17:25,085 --> 00:17:26,003
[suspicious music playing]

380
00:17:26,086 --> 00:17:31,759
That woman, Ms. Odette,
mentioned something.

381
00:17:31,842 --> 00:17:37,431
She said their former president's name

382
00:17:37,514 --> 00:17:39,808
was Kevin…

383
00:17:40,642 --> 00:17:41,685
Martinez!

384
00:17:41,769 --> 00:17:43,937
Kevin Martinez. That's his name.

385
00:17:44,646 --> 00:17:46,899
- Kevin Martinez.
- [Emerson] Mm-hmm.

386
00:17:47,733 --> 00:17:50,569
KM. So, he's Boss KM!

387
00:17:51,153 --> 00:17:53,572
- Oh, right.
- [Karla] Right?!

388
00:17:53,655 --> 00:17:55,199
[in English] Very good!

389
00:17:55,282 --> 00:17:57,743
Very good, you're right!

390
00:17:57,826 --> 00:18:00,621
He might really be
the mastermind behind the theft.

391
00:18:00,704 --> 00:18:01,955
You're amazing.

392
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:02,873
[Ame] Oh, no.

393
00:18:03,665 --> 00:18:06,376
We need to get the money from Boyet

394
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:08,796
before he gives it to KM!

395
00:18:09,963 --> 00:18:10,964
How?

396
00:18:12,216 --> 00:18:14,593
- [Kurt] Oh, call a friend again!
- Mmm, mmm, mmm.

397
00:18:14,676 --> 00:18:16,053
[Emerson] Enough, enough.

398
00:18:17,262 --> 00:18:18,180
I know.

399
00:18:19,264 --> 00:18:20,307
I got it.

400
00:18:21,475 --> 00:18:23,894
- [smirks]
- [action music playing]

401
00:18:27,439 --> 00:18:29,191
[line rings]

402
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:32,736
[in English] You look
as beautiful as ever.

403
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:35,322
[in English] Thank you. Um…

404
00:18:36,573 --> 00:18:39,201
[in English] I'm just dressed up today,

405
00:18:40,119 --> 00:18:42,913
because I'm actually waiting
for my boyfriend.

406
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:44,873
[pensive music playing]

407
00:18:44,957 --> 00:18:47,000
[in English] Uh, you don't have
a boyfriend.

408
00:18:48,335 --> 00:18:51,880
[in English] One coffee, one fork.

409
00:18:52,798 --> 00:18:53,799
[in English] Just you.

410
00:18:55,008 --> 00:18:56,385
[in English] What if he doesn't like cake?

411
00:18:58,137 --> 00:19:02,141
[in English] Look, maybe
we got off on the wrong foot.

412
00:19:02,891 --> 00:19:09,189
[in English] Uh, with the embassy and me
accusing you of stealing and breaking in.

413
00:19:09,857 --> 00:19:11,567
[in English] So, I'm sorry for that.

414
00:19:12,693 --> 00:19:15,279
[in English] So, does that mean that

415
00:19:15,863 --> 00:19:17,406
I'm not a suspect anymore?

416
00:19:17,489 --> 00:19:20,117
[in English] You are not a suspect,
no, no.

417
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:23,370
[in English] We actually have
a picture of the suspect.

418
00:19:24,705 --> 00:19:25,873
- [in English] Really?
- [Samir, in English] Yes.

419
00:19:25,956 --> 00:19:28,041
- [in English] How?
- [Samir clears throat, in English] AI.

420
00:19:29,084 --> 00:19:32,254
[in English] My men got footage from CCTV,

421
00:19:32,337 --> 00:19:36,008
and then we made a picture using AI.

422
00:19:36,091 --> 00:19:40,637
[suspicious music playing]

423
00:19:40,721 --> 00:19:44,183
[in English] This man
is a master of disguise.

424
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:47,227
[in English] He pretended to be
a window cleaner

425
00:19:47,311 --> 00:19:49,730
to sneak into the embassy.

426
00:19:50,689 --> 00:19:52,524
[music swells]

427
00:19:53,525 --> 00:19:54,985
[in English] Do you know this man?

428
00:19:55,068 --> 00:19:57,070
[tense music playing]

429
00:20:02,367 --> 00:20:04,161
[music intensifies]

430
00:20:04,244 --> 00:20:06,622
[Audrey, in English] No, no, no.
I… I got-- I got it.

431
00:20:06,705 --> 00:20:07,748
[Audrey clears throat]

432
00:20:09,166 --> 00:20:11,335
[pensive music playing]

433
00:20:11,418 --> 00:20:13,921
[in English] I'm sorry,
I'm… [chuckles] so embarrassed.

434
00:20:14,004 --> 00:20:15,464
[in English] I'm usually not this clumsy.

435
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:20,510
[in English] It's not because you maybe
recognized this man?

436
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:24,139
[in English] No. No, I don't know him. Um…

437
00:20:24,848 --> 00:20:28,018
[in English] You mentioned
that it's AI-generated, right?

438
00:20:28,101 --> 00:20:30,562
- [in English] Yes.
- [in English] So, doesn't that mean that

439
00:20:30,646 --> 00:20:33,607
there's a chance that maybe
the composition is wrong?

440
00:20:34,483 --> 00:20:35,734
[in English] I mean, come on.

441
00:20:35,817 --> 00:20:37,319
[in English] He's too handsome
to be a thief.

442
00:20:37,861 --> 00:20:40,489
[in English] He looks more
like a model, an actor.

443
00:20:41,156 --> 00:20:42,824
[in English] You know Dingdong Dantes?

444
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:45,577
[in English] Never heard of that man.

445
00:20:46,870 --> 00:20:51,208
[in English] But, um… maybe you're right.

446
00:20:52,626 --> 00:20:53,961
[in English] Or maybe you're wrong.

447
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:57,381
[in English] Anyway,
it was nice talking to you,

448
00:20:57,464 --> 00:21:00,467
but I really have to go.

449
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:04,304
[in English] Um, Ms. Audrey, maybe, um…

450
00:21:04,972 --> 00:21:06,974
I can have your phone number?

451
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:11,436
[in English] I can invite you
to some events at the embassy.

452
00:21:12,229 --> 00:21:13,647
[in English] I really
don't want to go back there

453
00:21:13,730 --> 00:21:15,524
after the robbery at the embassy,

454
00:21:15,607 --> 00:21:18,193
- and I'm still traumatized.
- [in English] Yes. How about, um…

455
00:21:18,777 --> 00:21:21,822
[in English] Maybe
we can go exercise, running?

456
00:21:21,905 --> 00:21:23,448
[in English] Uh, sometimes I go running

457
00:21:23,532 --> 00:21:26,326
in the Acacia Grove on Saturday.

458
00:21:26,410 --> 00:21:27,536
[in English] You've been there?

459
00:21:28,203 --> 00:21:30,289
[in English] No, never.

460
00:21:30,372 --> 00:21:31,873
[in English] Um… But yes, sure.

461
00:21:31,957 --> 00:21:33,166
[in English] Why not?

462
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:34,626
[in English] I mean, I gotta go. Okay?

463
00:21:34,710 --> 00:21:36,753
[in English] It was…
It was nice chatting with you.

464
00:21:38,422 --> 00:21:39,715
[in English] Ms. Audrey.

465
00:21:39,798 --> 00:21:41,174
[tense music playing]

466
00:21:42,884 --> 00:21:43,760
[in English] Your phone number.

467
00:21:44,386 --> 00:21:47,014
[in English] Oh, I'm sorry. I… I forgot.

468
00:21:49,266 --> 00:21:50,100
‪Um…

469
00:21:54,313 --> 00:21:55,314
[in English] There you go.

470
00:21:55,981 --> 00:21:56,773
[in English] I gotta go.

471
00:21:56,857 --> 00:21:58,275
- [Samir, in English] Goodbye.
- [in English] Bye!

472
00:21:58,358 --> 00:22:00,360
[music swells]

473
00:22:06,867 --> 00:22:08,452
[music fades]

474
00:22:08,535 --> 00:22:10,871
[muffled chattering in the distance]

475
00:22:10,954 --> 00:22:11,955
[in English] Hello, everybody!

476
00:22:13,290 --> 00:22:14,499
[Atoy, in English] So, I see
no other way for you

477
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:16,043
to intercept the package,

478
00:22:16,126 --> 00:22:18,754
but for you to be present at the auction.

479
00:22:19,379 --> 00:22:23,175
Wow, your voice is making me swoon, Atoy!

480
00:22:23,258 --> 00:22:25,135
[in English] Ame, this is serious.

481
00:22:25,844 --> 00:22:28,805
[in English] Your mission
is to retrieve the package

482
00:22:28,889 --> 00:22:30,807
with the five million pesos in it.

483
00:22:31,892 --> 00:22:35,103
[Atoy] <i>Let's assume the auction venue</i>
<i>is heavily guarded.</i>

484
00:22:35,187 --> 00:22:38,023
Of course, because
expensive items will be there.

485
00:22:38,106 --> 00:22:39,858
[in English] Uh, copy that, Atoy.

486
00:22:39,941 --> 00:22:43,445
[Atoy] <i>Someone needs to pose</i>
<i>as a buyer attending the auction.</i>

487
00:22:44,362 --> 00:22:47,115
<i>You need to look rich.</i>

488
00:22:47,199 --> 00:22:51,328
The type who can spend millions
on a single item.

489
00:22:52,204 --> 00:22:55,040
But not all of you can be buyers.

490
00:22:55,123 --> 00:22:57,292
Some of you need to be the eyes and ears.

491
00:22:57,375 --> 00:22:59,711
[Atoy] <i>And of course, someone</i>
<i>must be assigned as a distraction</i>

492
00:22:59,795 --> 00:23:01,421
<i>if things don't go according to plan.</i>

493
00:23:02,422 --> 00:23:03,256
[in English] Copy?

494
00:23:03,340 --> 00:23:05,050
We know what you mean, Atoy.

495
00:23:05,133 --> 00:23:06,384
We can handle this.

496
00:23:06,468 --> 00:23:07,302
[in English] Very good.

497
00:23:08,095 --> 00:23:11,556
By the way, how many of you are there?
Who's with you?

498
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:12,724
Uh…

499
00:23:12,808 --> 00:23:16,353
Me, Ame, Brother Kurt,

500
00:23:16,853 --> 00:23:19,189
and Karla, and we are the…

501
00:23:19,731 --> 00:23:21,775
Children of the Thread.

502
00:23:21,858 --> 00:23:23,443
See? It's good, right?

503
00:23:23,527 --> 00:23:25,320
Nice, right? It's nice. I thought of it.

504
00:23:25,403 --> 00:23:26,321
I thought of it.

505
00:23:26,404 --> 00:23:27,239
Fine, fine.

506
00:23:27,322 --> 00:23:28,156
- All right.
- I thought of it.

507
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:29,199
- We'll give it to you.
- Hmm.

508
00:23:29,282 --> 00:23:30,617
Did you say Karla?

509
00:23:31,118 --> 00:23:32,494
[Kurt] Why not?

510
00:23:33,995 --> 00:23:35,622
The more the merrier.

511
00:23:35,705 --> 00:23:37,624
Don't bring Karla.

512
00:23:37,707 --> 00:23:39,668
[pensive music playing]

513
00:23:39,751 --> 00:23:42,003
Hey. Oh, Karla!

514
00:23:43,588 --> 00:23:46,049
Uh, um…

515
00:23:46,133 --> 00:23:47,759
Okay, ‘Toy…

516
00:23:47,843 --> 00:23:48,844
I'll handle it.

517
00:23:48,927 --> 00:23:51,471
We'll fix this. We'll update you.

518
00:23:52,597 --> 00:23:53,473
[in English] Okay.

519
00:23:53,557 --> 00:23:55,016
[pensive music playing]

520
00:23:58,728 --> 00:23:59,938
[Emerson] Karla.

521
00:24:00,522 --> 00:24:01,481
Poor Karla.

522
00:24:01,565 --> 00:24:02,566
I told you.

523
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:07,279
Hey. Are you okay?

524
00:24:08,613 --> 00:24:10,615
Of course not. You walked out.

525
00:24:11,825 --> 00:24:13,160
I was happy for a moment.

526
00:24:13,243 --> 00:24:15,245
I heard Brother Atoy's voice.

527
00:24:15,328 --> 00:24:17,664
At least I knew he was safe. He's okay.

528
00:24:18,290 --> 00:24:21,001
But is he really that upset with me?

529
00:24:21,084 --> 00:24:23,128
He barred me from the mission?

530
00:24:24,087 --> 00:24:26,423
You're too sensitive.

531
00:24:26,506 --> 00:24:28,258
You're too sensitive.

532
00:24:28,341 --> 00:24:29,843
[melancholic music playing]

533
00:24:29,926 --> 00:24:31,011
[Emerson] Look.

534
00:24:31,678 --> 00:24:32,846
You know…

535
00:24:33,972 --> 00:24:37,058
I understand Atoy
because he's your brother.

536
00:24:37,642 --> 00:24:38,685
If it were me…

537
00:24:39,311 --> 00:24:42,439
If Tonet were here,

538
00:24:42,522 --> 00:24:46,902
I wouldn't let her join
dangerous missions either.

539
00:24:47,485 --> 00:24:48,403
I don't want her to get hurt.

540
00:24:48,486 --> 00:24:51,072
She's my sister. I love her.

541
00:24:52,157 --> 00:24:54,034
But if Sis Tonet were here,

542
00:24:54,659 --> 00:24:56,494
she'd want you to be together, right?

543
00:24:57,537 --> 00:24:59,372
At least you'd be sure you're both safe.

544
00:24:59,456 --> 00:25:02,751
[pensive music playing]

545
00:25:04,377 --> 00:25:05,670
Please, brother.

546
00:25:05,754 --> 00:25:07,964
Include me, please.

547
00:25:08,048 --> 00:25:11,426
I don't want to be left behind,
just worrying about you.

548
00:25:11,509 --> 00:25:13,386
I promise, I can help.

549
00:25:13,470 --> 00:25:15,388
You're so persistent.

550
00:25:15,472 --> 00:25:18,141
I'll get scolded by Atoy.
He'll be mad at me.

551
00:25:18,767 --> 00:25:20,227
Here's the plan, brother.

552
00:25:20,310 --> 00:25:22,270
Let's not tell Brother Atoy.

553
00:25:22,354 --> 00:25:24,648
He doesn't need to know, right?

554
00:25:24,731 --> 00:25:26,233
[suspicious music playing]

555
00:25:26,316 --> 00:25:28,777
Come on, I'll help.

556
00:25:31,821 --> 00:25:36,534
[electronic blipping]

557
00:25:36,618 --> 00:25:41,039
[tense music playing]

558
00:25:42,415 --> 00:25:44,042
Do we really need suspenders?

559
00:25:44,125 --> 00:25:46,002
It's our brand identity!

560
00:25:46,086 --> 00:25:48,338
We need to look solid
for our first mission.

561
00:25:48,421 --> 00:25:51,675
Operation Suitcase.

562
00:25:51,758 --> 00:25:53,468
Is Atoy here?

563
00:25:53,551 --> 00:25:55,804
I wanted to ask permission from him.

564
00:25:55,887 --> 00:25:57,889
We're going to the US.

565
00:25:57,973 --> 00:26:00,058
- Vacation?
- [in English] Maybe for good.

566
00:26:00,141 --> 00:26:01,268
[screaming and panicking]

567
00:26:01,351 --> 00:26:03,979
[thumping and groaning]

568
00:26:04,062 --> 00:26:05,689
UP NEXT

569
00:26:05,772 --> 00:26:06,731
No kids allowed here.

570
00:26:06,815 --> 00:26:10,151
Help me. They're going to kill my mom!

571
00:26:10,735 --> 00:26:11,820
Mama!

572
00:26:11,903 --> 00:26:12,862
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

573
00:26:12,946 --> 00:26:14,239
[grunts]

574
00:26:16,366 --> 00:26:17,826
[security officer, in English]
Our intel told us

575
00:26:17,909 --> 00:26:20,870
that the decoder of this town
is the mayor's niece.

576
00:26:20,954 --> 00:26:21,871
[in English] So, she might be here.

577
00:26:21,955 --> 00:26:26,126
[in English] This is the man who
brought him to the ambassador's office.

578
00:26:26,209 --> 00:26:28,837
[Samir, in English] Here.
He might be here too.

579
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:30,505
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

580
00:26:30,588 --> 00:26:33,883
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

581
00:26:33,967 --> 00:26:35,343
♪ <i>Fix this</i> ♪

582
00:26:35,427 --> 00:26:36,469
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
